        "author_association": "MEMBER",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nTracking issue for migrating all apps off the shared API pattern (`api` repo) onto individual K8s deployments. Each app gets its own backend deployment on AKS. Once all apps are migrated, the shared API Container App and the `api` repo's route-aggregation role are decommissioned.\n\n## App migration issues\n\n- [x] nelsong6/my-homepage#22\n- [x] nelsong6/kill-me#14\n- [x] nelsong6/house-hunt#1\n- [x] nelsong6/investing#6\n- [x] nelsong6/plant-agent#10\n- [ ] nelsong6/api#14\n\n## Shared-api route package splits (discovered mid-migration)\n\nWith the four app backends migrated, the shared api still hosts route packages owned by other repos (`/fzt`, `/ci`, `/llm`). These should move to their owning repos as their own k8s deployments before #23 can fully retire the api container.\n\n- [x] nelsong6/fzt-frontend#5 — /fzt/tree/:id to fzt-frontend.romaine.life\n- [x] nelsong6/diagrams#14 — /ci/* consolidated behind docs.romaine.life\n- [x] nelsong6/llm-explorer#1 — /llm/* to llm-explorer.romaine.life\n\n## Completion criteria\n\nAll checkboxes above are done. Then proceed with #23 (Decommission ACA + SWA).\n\n## Depends on\n\n- #17 (ingress controller)\n- #18 (cert-manager)\n- #19 (ExternalSecrets)\n- #20 (ExternalDNS)\n- #22 (first app migration — proves the stack)\n\n## Risk profile\n\nPersonal portfolio — no external users, SLAs, or paging. Migrate with confidence: direct cutover, no canary windows, no rollback rehearsals. If something breaks, iterate. Blast radius is zero. Don't over-engineer this.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",
